            "name": "List the currently configured logical repositories.\nA logical repository is a set of rules to match PRs, releases, and deployments\nthat has a name and pretends to be a regular GitHub repository everywhere in UI\nand API requests.\nThis feature is particularly useful to reap monorepos into separate, joint or disjoint\nparts.\n",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{ server_url }}/v1/settings/logical_repositories/:id",
